      "writtenOn": "2018-05-03T05:25:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "sstx and ssrx are the USB superspeed transmit and receive pairs\nml is the DisplayPort Main Link. Called \"L\" in the comments above.\nUp to four lanes total, so DP case connects them all and dock connects 2 DP and USB.\n\na2, a3, a10, a11, b2, b3, b10, b11 are pins on the USB-C connector. \n\nNote sw_sel is written to two registers, each bit makes one connection\n\nI don\u0027t understand why the value here is 0x21. I believe it should be 0x20,\notherwise this is identical to the TYPEC_MUX_DOCK case and you will connect DisplayPort on to the pins that should be unused, which is a violation of the spec (and will cause issues if the other end happens to be a USB3.2 device capable of x2 operation where these lanes would carry USB signalling). (I know the bug says to use 0x21 but it seems wrong)",
      "parentUuid": "682be093_f39f00b0",
